    "created_at": "2015-09-09T16:07:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-09T16:07:14Z",
    "body": "The diff corresponds to when implementers referred the [CSS Ruby spec](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-ruby/#default-stylesheet), as it's changing quite often and quite drastically. Gecko implemented after the last large refactor of the spec, so it's most up-to-date.\n\nI'm not familiar with how much copy of CSS specs HTML spec should have. Is it possible to simply delegate to CSS Ruby as it's still WD and is possibly to evolve further? That makes CSS spec editors a bit happier to maintain single copy.\n\nOr do we want to have the minimum common denominator in HTML spec?\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
